# The Status sync row while a config replay is still running.
#
# The row used to say "in progress" and nothing else for as long as a sync took, which on a
# 135-node radio is about seventeen seconds - and on a link that kept dropping mid-roster it said
# it forever, because each reconnect started the replay again from nothing. That is the state
# this scene is a picture of: the count is what tells a sync that is working from one that has
# stalled, and it is the reason the roster is now kept across a drop rather than re-fetched.
#
# `config` first so the card has a radio to describe, then `syncing` puts the replay back in
# flight partway through - the two are ordered, not interchangeable.
scene demo
scale 4
clock 2026-01-12 19:12
config
stats
syncing
tab status
